WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.000
<i>Higashida...</i>

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.000
<i>Higashida...</i>

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:07.920
<i>Daisuke Higashida...</i>

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:11.720
<i>It seems like the time has come
for us to part ways...</i>

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:12.880
<i>or something like that...</i>

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.180
<i>This may be goodbye...
or something like that...</i>

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.140
<i>How can I put it? It's like...</i>

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:19.770
<i>We're breaking up. I mean... It's like...</i>

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.020
Appear after you know
what you wanna say!

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:30.190
THERE'S A REASON FOR EVERYTHING

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:28.530
The old man appeared in your dream?

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.360
What does that mean?

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:31.700
I don't know.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.820
Going by his words, we're probably
not going to see each other again.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.370
Really?

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:39.700
Without that guy, if we go over there,
we won't be able to come back.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:40.790
Then don't go there.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:43.500
But... I see...

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:47.380
What's wrong? It looks like
you're using your non-existent brain.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:52.920
I feel like something is changing
when I'm with the old man.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.220
How can I put it?

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:56.800
A little more...

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.760
Just a little more...

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.060
and I'll grab your stomach!

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:02.930
Don't you mean crush it?

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:06.650
Please don't brood over it.
A storm will come.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.440
Come to think of it,
the last time I went to see him,

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.320
you two were having
a conversation, right?

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:12.860
What were you talking about?

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.410
<i>Sweethearts...</i>

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:18.120
Well, you know...

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:20.830
Relations between males and females...

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:24.000
You mean like what you would learn
about in health class?

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:25.790
Miyakoshi...

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:30.340
That would never happen with us.
That would never happen with us.

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:32.210
Why do you have to say it twice?

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:34.590
Oh? Did I say it twice?

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:38.550
Please don't think of weird things,
whatever they are.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:40.680
As long as there's the chocolate
and the cooking,

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:42.890
we can keep going out normally like this.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:46.390
Um...

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:48.020
Huh?

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:51.980
<i>Wha... I just said something to the effect
that I want to go out with Miyakoshi!</i>

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:53.900
<i>Don't tell me
that on a subconscious level...</i>

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:56.650
<i>Calm down.
Stay cool in front of Miyakoshi.</i>

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:59.280
<i>Watch for her response
and then act accordingly.</i>

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:58.110
BEEP

00:01:58.410 --> 00:01:59.870
BZZZ

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:01.870
<i>Her brain hasn't caught up
with the processing.</i>

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:01.870
BEEP

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.790
Like, I don't really get it,

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.920
but the gist is that my cooking
is on the verge of success!

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.250
I can't just stand around and chat!

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:09.500
Miyakoshi, wait!

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:13.170
After I finish all my work, I'm going
right home to think about cooking!

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:14.630
That's ridiculously impressive!

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:20.100
Really, please do not force-feed me
something awful

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:23.100
and do everything you can to ruin me.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:24.520
Wait a second!

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:28.650
Higashida, you think I'm someone who
force-feeds people dangerous substances?

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:29.690
I sure as hell do!

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:30.940
Wha...? Needless anger!

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:32.070
Righteous anger!

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:33.780
ANYONE CAN MASTER POPULAR HOME COOKING
AND MAKE IT DELICIOUS!

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:35.240
HMMM HMMM

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:38.200
I feel like I'm close to a breakthrough.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.950
<i>Think back to what Muranushi
and old man Valentine said.</i>

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:44.830
<i>But Higashida...</i>

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:46.660
<i>But Higashida... When I think about it,
it is kind of impressive</i>

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:49.670
<i>that he's been my voluntary
taste-tester all this time.</i>

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:55.670
That's right. I have to cook something
decent for Higashida's sake, too.

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:58.010
What should I do?

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:01.550
My cooking sucks,
which is exactly why I have to do it.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:05.560
With consideration,
thinking about the other person...

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:08.690
When I'm cooking...
think about the person eating...

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:10.480
Tasting!

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:14.150
<i>This is bad. Now Miyakoshi
is enthusiastic about cooking.</i>

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:17.440
<i>I have a feeling she'll force
a dish on me today,</i>

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:19.200
<i>so I'd better try to change the subject.</i>

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.160
What's wrong, Miyakoshi?

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:24.910
Miyakoshi...

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.120
I was wondering who you were.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:28.790
Are you all right?

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:31.540
Your eyes are lifeless,
and you're drooling.

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:33.040
A hero...

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.090
Are you okay?

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:37.090
It seems like you've eaten
your own cooking.

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:39.840
Or, no. The results of that
would be even worse than this.

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:41.840
Don't ask me anything.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:44.680
Right now, I'm ashamed
to look you in the face.

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:47.890
Your eyes are out of focus,
so you can't look me in the face.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:51.100
I have my own battle to fight.

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:52.350
Miyakoshi...

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:54.810
ONE WEEK LATER

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:54.020
Miyakoshi?

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:57.900
Sorry I made you walk me home.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.570
No, that's fine.

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:04.780
SHIVER SHIVER

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:04.780
<i>Chaos...</i>

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:07.370
Maybe this is Miyakoshi's...

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:16.130
Cooking, huh?
You were cooking, weren't you?

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.840
Yeah. Higashida, I was cooking your...

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.800
Miyakoshi, calm down.
For now, let's go inside.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:31.100
This miasma is from your cooking, huh?

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.480
I... I...

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:37.020
Living in a place like this
would give anyone a mental disorder.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.360
My cooking...

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:40.070
- I tasted it.
- Tasted it?

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:42.070
<i>She was that reckless?</i>

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:43.240
Tasted it?

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:44.030
<i>Or, she's only started tasting
her own cooking at this point?</i>

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:46.280
<i>Or just tasting her cooking led
to a disaster of epic proportions?</i>

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:46.280
Tasted it?

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:47.700
<i>I don't know which one
to answer her with.</i>

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:49.580
Why would you do something like that?

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:53.960
T-To make delicious cooking,
I thought of the person eating it...

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:54.790
Tasting it...

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:58.340
And after tasting it, I understood.

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:00.630
I'm no good, as a cook
or a human being.

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:05.050
I was fine with making someone
eat this stuff all this time.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:06.260
Making you eat it, Higashida...

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:12.770
SOB SOB SOB

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:10.850
Higashida, I'm sorry! I'm so sorry!

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:12.770
For now, please stop crying.
This is awkward.

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:13.980
RUB RUB RUB

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:17.480
But it seems you've finally
realized the error of your ways.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:20.190
Yeah. I'm done cooking.

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:24.530
That being said, you've already
caused me enough damage to kill me,

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:27.280
so maybe I'll have you compensate me.

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:29.410
I-If it's something I can do...

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:32.950
For starters, I think I'll have you
make me something to eat!

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:35.790
H-Higashida, what do you mean by that?

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:38.420
Nothing. I'm just hungry. Hurry up!

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:40.840
Easy to say, but I've done
nothing but fail at it...

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:44.380
The only thing that looked like
it was supposed to was the chocolate.

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:45.340
Hurry up!

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:48.680
Are you really gonna eat it?

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:50.470
It's chocolate of all things.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:52.850
Actually, chocolate is perfect.

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:57.270
It's fitting that this is your
last dish, Miyakoshi.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:06:00.730
I'm going to take a big bite,
then pay my respects to Valentine.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:02.690
H-Higashida...

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:04.650
Here I go.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:14.540
CHOKE

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.000
Disgusting!

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:16.460
- Disgusting?
- Disgusting?

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:18.290
What does that mean?

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:21.130
Miyakoshi chocolate is only disgusting?

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:22.800
You're not going to see the old man?

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:23.550
Then...

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:24.300
KILL

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:25.510
Then I've finally killed you!

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:26.260
I'm not dead.

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:29.930
<i>Both of you...</i>

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:34.720
<i>Old man...</i>

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:36.640
<i>You've done well.</i>

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:40.900
<i>Your consideration for each other
has worked a miracle.</i>

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:44.440
<i>You no longer have to do your best,
with your life on the line.</i>

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:47.070
<i>I see... We...</i>

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:49.200
<i>We're already dead.</i>

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:52.530
<i>Stop! You're not dead!
Neither of you are dead!</i>

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:55.080
<i>I just set the mood
and started talking to you is all!</i>

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:59.080
<i>You two don't need
to go to that world anymore.</i>

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:04.130
<i>I made an effort to come to this world
so I could say goodbye.</i>

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:05.260
<i>Old man...</i>

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:08.220
<i>Yes, yes. You really did your best, Hana.</i>

00:07:08.510 --> 00:07:09.550
<i>You, too, Higashi.</i>

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:10.680
<i>I'm moved.</i>

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:12.970
<i>I can't tell from the expression
on your face.</i>

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:16.390
<i>And so this really is goodbye.</i>

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:17.270
<i>Old man...</i>

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:19.890
<i>Hana, you impressed me in the end.</i>

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:22.440
<i>Never forget to be considerate
of the other person.</i>

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:23.270
<i>Okay.</i>

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:26.530
<i>And give up on cooking already.</i>

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:27.400
<i>I really should?</i>

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:28.900
<i>Higashi...</i>

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:32.620
<i>you've been through a lot, and you're not
at all like what you used to be,</i>

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:33.580
<i>but don't worry about it.</i>

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:35.620
<i>Please give me more encouraging words.</i>

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:39.460
<i>I don't know what's going to happen
with you two, but for now, get along.</i>

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:42.420
<i>Love and peace.</i>

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:57.060
How can I put it? It's over, huh?

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:58.810
Good job.

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:00.140
Well, I'm going home.

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:01.390
Higashida...

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.560
It's okay. I'm touched.

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:07.570
Wh-Wh-What's your type of woman?

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:10.780
What do you mean, what's my type?

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:16.660
Y-You know, like, for example...
l-long hair or short hair...

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:18.700
Hair? Hair, huh?

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:21.750
Maybe long?

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:24.580
I can grow it out, right?
I can grow it out!

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:25.420
See you!

00:08:34.390 --> 00:08:38.890
SIX MONTHS LATER

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:38.470
Thank you!

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:41.390
Miyakoshi's hair has really gotten long!

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:42.480
Yeah.

00:08:43.310 --> 00:08:45.360
And your hair's short now, Naga.

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:46.940
That's because I got a haircut.

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:49.530
It seems Higashi likes long hair.

00:08:49.530 --> 00:08:51.490
Miyakoshi is cute, isn't she?

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:54.660
And the day after you heard that,
you got a haircut.

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:56.910
I-It was just a coincidence!

00:08:56.910 --> 00:09:00.080
I had an appointment at the hairdresser
before I heard about that.

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:01.540
So it's a total coincidence!

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:03.500
Then why did you get a short haircut?

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:08.880
I-I did it because you and I
had the same hairstyle, Yanagiba.

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:12.090
Actually, it feels like
I was in love with Higashida

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:15.510
out of a sense of duty
from the very beginning.

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:17.550
But I've totally given up on him.

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:20.470
Next time, I'm going to have
an easier romance.

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:22.060
I hope!

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:24.690
And you don't have any regrets?

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:25.810
Regrets?

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:31.150
REFRESHED

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:28.650
I absolutely, positively
don't have a single one!

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:31.150
Naga, you're too refreshed.

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:34.150
But I'm glad that I became
a regular at this restaurant.

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:38.120
Because I made a friend
I can talk to every day.

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:39.620
Naga...

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:43.910
I'm glad I made friends
with you too, Naga.

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:47.630
I'm glad I made friends with someone
who goes to the same school.

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:51.920
I... I've decided...

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:52.960
You're coming to school?

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:55.050
...to give up on the idea of going there.

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:56.340
Huh?

00:09:56.890 --> 00:10:01.100
Naga is even cuter
after getting her haircut.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:03.100
Stay away from high school students!

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:06.690
That's right. Being frivolous
when you're working is improper.

00:10:06.690 --> 00:10:10.360
At work, work hard,
not romp in the flowers.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:12.360
Shut up. I'll mow you down, little girl.

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:13.820
AREA TO BE MOWED

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:15.490
SLASH SLASH SLASH

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:18.240
Saiki, your Japanese has really improved.

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:23.410
Kamakura told me to say that to Kisaki
if she said something to me.

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:27.040
I'm glad you've become
a decent worker, Saiki.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:31.090
Cause with part-time jobs, you never
know when someone's gonna quit.

00:10:31.090 --> 00:10:32.340
You're right.

00:10:34.550 --> 00:10:36.420
One person has quit recently, right?

00:10:37.090 --> 00:10:38.260
Yuuta!

00:10:39.090 --> 00:10:40.180
Hello.

00:10:40.180 --> 00:10:42.470
I figured you were coming.
The flowers were blooming.

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:43.390
They were blooming.

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:45.350
Thanks.

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:47.480
- Yuuta!
- Shiho, stay back!

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:50.980
I'm covered in mud, so if you hug me,
your uniform will get dirty.

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:53.440
I'll bring your lunch!

00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:57.530
Good thing
Kamakura moved back home, huh?

00:10:57.530 --> 00:10:58.320
Yeah.

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:00.910
She's really changed.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:03.950
The blooming flowers
have become a Shindou radar.

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:09.920
HA HA HA HA

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:06.660
Sometimes they're blooming
from morning on.

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:08.710
Sometimes they're blooming
from morning on.

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:12.750
But it must be tough for you,
starting so early in the morning.

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:15.630
Oh, right. But it's the construction
industry, so...

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:18.590
Shiho's dad pulled strings.

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:20.840
It's a tough job, but the pay is good,

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:24.100
and it comes regularly,
so I've been able to quit being a host.

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:26.850
But I often find myself
on crumbling scaffolding.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:28.850
That's a dangerous job!

00:11:29.310 --> 00:11:32.270
And sometimes there are
unnatural breaks in the ropes.

00:11:32.270 --> 00:11:34.610
Dishonest businesses are black,
but yours is blood-colored!

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:36.990
Yuuta, I've brought your lunch.

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:38.610
Great. Well, see you again.

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:39.780
See you!

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:43.620
Today and tomorrow, too,
work hard and make money.

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:44.700
Here.

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:48.460
Between my dad using his tuna-fishing
earnings on pachinko and my own pay,

00:11:48.460 --> 00:11:52.130
I don't know whether we're in the black
or red overall, but I'll do my best.

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:53.590
I-I will...

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:56.800
also do my best to learn
about society by working part-time

00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:59.220
so I can become a wife deserving of you.

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:02.300
Sometimes I help out in the kitchen
and learn how to cook, too!

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:04.100
Yuuta...

00:12:04.350 --> 00:12:06.850
Recently, this is the only place
where we've been meeting,

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:09.680
and I can change my uniform, so, um...

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:13.980
Okay.

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:17.690
THUMP THUMP

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:16.190
Yuuta...

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:19.280
Yuuta!

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:23.780
Oh, the voice from heaven is telling me
to hurry up and make money,

00:12:23.780 --> 00:12:25.830
so we'll continue next time, okay?

00:12:25.830 --> 00:12:30.370
I see. I guess it's our fate
to have money come between us.

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:32.120
What are you talking about?

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:35.380
Without money,
we never would've met, right?

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:39.340
Y-Yuuta! That was so cool!

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:42.010
I'll see you.

00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:45.220
<i>I embarrass myself every time
with these corny lines!</i>

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:47.470
Okay! I'll see you later, Yuuta!

00:12:47.930 --> 00:12:49.810
Yeah! See you later!

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:58.190
Our lady used to be such a sadist,
but now she's a flower garden.

00:12:58.440 --> 00:13:00.150
That worries me, too.

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:04.160
I think it's fine. It's most important
for people to be honest about their feelings.

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:07.030
I'll hold the fort. Go ahead, Adachi.

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:08.910
Oh, okay.

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:10.200
Sorry, Kouno.

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:11.750
It's fine. Don't worry about it!

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:16.130
But I guess as your friend,
I'll see you off with a note of caution.

00:13:16.670 --> 00:13:18.290
We're short on knives in the kitchen.

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:23.840
S-Sorry I had you change
your break so we could talk.

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:26.550
That's no big deal. What is it?

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:28.640
Um... Uh...

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:30.270
It's kind of important.

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:33.810
So what is it?

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:37.610
Um, I'm thinking of quitting.

00:13:41.110 --> 00:13:43.700
My family runs a sushi restaurant,
so I thought it was about time.

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:45.780
I mean, I need to get serious
about the family business.

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:47.700
<i>A second one!</i>

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:49.120
<i>I'm scared.</i>

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:51.040
And if I get serious
about my family's restaurant,

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:55.250
I'll be busy from early in the morning
until night, so it won't be like it's been.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:58.340
I see. Never mind here at work...

00:13:58.340 --> 00:14:01.090
we'd hardly be able to see
each other even on days off, huh?

00:14:01.090 --> 00:14:02.130
That could be.

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:03.630
<i>A third knife?</i>

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:07.970
Muranushi, you'll understand
when I tell you. I mean, let me finish...

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:11.560
I don't want to be unable to see you.

00:14:12.270 --> 00:14:12.890
Muranushi...

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:13.560
Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:29.070
CRUSH CRUSH

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:18.860
I don't want to resolve something serious
during a break at my part-time job.

00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:22.570
Well, I thought it would be easier
if we talked here.

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:23.320
About what?

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:27.030
Um, well, this was just a proposal.
How can I put it?

00:14:27.030 --> 00:14:30.200
Like, if it's impossible for you,
Muranushi, then there's nothing for it.

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:31.370
Again, what is it?

00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:34.080
Muranushi, would you quit here
and come to my place?

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:36.290
That's a no?

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:39.080
What do you... What do you mean?

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:43.170
U-Um, I want to see you more,
and we have an empty room at my house,

00:14:43.170 --> 00:14:47.340
so I thought maybe you could stay there
while working at the restaurant.

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:53.060
<i>I lost consciousness for a moment.</i>

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:57.390
Adachi. Are you okay?

00:14:57.640 --> 00:15:01.110
Huh? Maybe I'm not okay so much...

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:03.110
Sorry, that hurts, doesn't it?

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:08.240
That's fine, but explain how your
thinking jumped to that conclusion.

00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:12.830
U-Um, normally a guy would
probably propose at a time like this,

00:15:12.830 --> 00:15:15.620
but I'm still too inexperienced
to take over the family business,

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:19.080
so given the circumstances,
that would only put a burden on you.

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:22.500
That being said,
I don't want to be apart from you,

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:26.800
so I want you to watch over me
until I do have my act together.

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:28.760
<i>The person I'm in love with...</i>

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:31.180
You'd kind of be there to keep me in line.

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:34.600
<i>...is really scary
when he's driven into a corner.</i>

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:38.140
<i>And I missed out on the timing to blush.</i>

00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:41.600
That being said,
I'm still a college student

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:45.230
and I don't think
my mom would let me do that.

00:15:45.780 --> 00:15:48.110
Yeah, true. You can answer that.

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:49.110
MOM

00:15:49.450 --> 00:15:50.820
It's fine with me.

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:53.660
I don't think she would let me.

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:56.200
A-Are you sure it was okay
to just hang up like that?

00:15:56.410 --> 00:15:59.460
Well, my break is over, so there it is.

00:15:59.460 --> 00:16:00.710
Right.

00:16:01.750 --> 00:16:02.750
<i>No good, huh?</i>

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:07.420
The sentiment makes me happy.

00:16:07.760 --> 00:16:11.010
I'll start by working there part-time,
so I'll need a lot of guidance.

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:11.760
The rest...

00:16:12.470 --> 00:16:13.800
we'll take a step at a time.

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:15.680
You smiled...

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:20.270
No, I didn't. Don't expect much
in the way of affection.

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:24.360
Right. Then before you change
your mind, let's go tell the manager.

00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:29.400
Is that why you had us talk in the break
room about something important?

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:30.240
That's right.

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:33.200
Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:34.200
PINCH PINCH

00:16:30.610 --> 00:16:33.740
We'll work on that personality
a step at a time, too.

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:36.410
CONGRATULATIONS

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:35.740
Mama!

00:16:35.990 --> 00:16:38.580
Mama!

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:40.370
Mama...

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:42.960
Sorry. Come here.

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:44.750
I was distracted
by the supernatural phenomenon.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:45.840
Did something happen?

00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:47.800
It's hard to explain.

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:50.380
Sakaki... This is just a hunch,

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:54.510
but I think the restaurant is going to
lose a lot of its workforce before long.

00:16:56.550 --> 00:16:57.390
Mishter...

00:16:57.390 --> 00:16:59.930
Anyway, Hime sure has grown.

00:17:00.180 --> 00:17:03.440
She can stand now
and is starting to say a few words.

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:05.440
Mishter Sakaki, money!

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:07.440
She says that word especially clearly.

00:17:07.730 --> 00:17:10.690
Money, money, money!

00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:11.900
Don't chant it!

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:15.660
It seems she's gotten into investing
and the habit of making money.

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:16.530
Habit?

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:20.040
But I'm reminded all the time
of how tough it is raising a kid.

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:22.870
I guess she needs a father.

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:24.870
Are you going to take him back?

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:28.250
Yeah, right. I don't even see him.

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:29.920
But even if it's impossible now,

00:17:30.170 --> 00:17:32.840
I'll have to let Hime
meet him sometime.

00:17:33.170 --> 00:17:35.430
When she's in that rebellious stage.

00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:38.140
<i>She has various complicated
feelings about it, huh?</i>

00:17:38.470 --> 00:17:42.140
Don't worry about Hime.
Do your best with your own work.

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:43.310
Oh, right.

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:47.480
As the manager,
I'd like you to do your job, Kisaki.

00:17:49.070 --> 00:17:50.940
- Fine.
- Right?

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:54.030
Did you just agree to work? Kisaki!

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:56.160
- Did something happen?
- Not especially.

00:17:56.160 --> 00:17:56.910
Come to think of it,

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:59.330
your bangs have grown out, Kisaki.

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:00.660
You notice that now?

00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:02.370
They've always been long.

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:05.290
You seem different.

00:18:05.290 --> 00:18:06.170
Never mind me.

00:18:06.170 --> 00:18:09.250
Isn't there someone else
you should be saying those words to?

00:18:10.420 --> 00:18:12.130
<i>Easy for her to say...</i>

00:18:14.970 --> 00:18:17.090
All right! Success!

00:18:17.300 --> 00:18:18.930
<i>She hasn't changed at all.</i>

00:18:19.180 --> 00:18:22.140
Miyakoshi, did you make
instant noodles again?

00:18:22.390 --> 00:18:24.560
I'm sick of seeing that miracle.

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:27.520
Don't sit down next to me
all of a sudden!

00:18:27.850 --> 00:18:29.270
A-Anyway...

00:18:29.770 --> 00:18:33.230
When it comes to cooking,
the little good things are important!

00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:38.240
There were a lot of sad incidents,
but good things too, weren't there?

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:40.700
Wh-What?

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:45.870
For example, when your cooking
drove your home into a state of chaos,

00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:48.580
your mother looked to your father
for help, and they reconciled.

00:18:48.580 --> 00:18:52.380
I'm happy for them, but personally,
it's a little embarrassing!

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:55.090
- Miyakoshi...
- Wh-Wh-What?

00:18:55.550 --> 00:18:57.300
I've thought this for a while now...

00:18:57.930 --> 00:18:59.260
Shall we break up?

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:06.180
Saying something
as serious as that so lightly...

00:19:06.770 --> 00:19:09.150
You said it
without any kind of preamble.

00:19:09.770 --> 00:19:11.900
And without any expression
on your face.

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:14.110
H-How cruel can you be?

00:19:14.440 --> 00:19:17.990
Who did it? Who made you like that?

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:20.030
I did!

00:19:21.070 --> 00:19:23.950
Now I know what redistribution feels like.

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:25.660
That's "retribution."

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:27.790
So... can I go on?

00:19:27.790 --> 00:19:28.920
Y-Yeah.

00:19:29.170 --> 00:19:31.750
I've caused you a lot of problems.

00:19:32.380 --> 00:19:34.630
I can't stop you.

00:19:35.300 --> 00:19:38.050
Then we broke up, a clean break.

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:44.470
Go out with me.

00:19:47.390 --> 00:19:51.560
Up to now, our relationship has been
for the sake of curing your cooking disease,

00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:55.280
but now that it's solved, I broke up
with you to put a period on all that.

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:56.860
And now, starting over...

00:19:58.070 --> 00:19:59.110
Higashida...

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:02.450
Higashida...

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:08.540
You were watching me for like a minute
while I was depressed, right? Right?

00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:10.170
I was watching you. It was funny.

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:14.790
I-I don't get your
change of heart or whatever it is...

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:17.380
Right, that.
I'll explain it in a simple way.

00:20:17.380 --> 00:20:22.640
APRIL

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:19.920
After the final cooking incident,

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:22.640
to be honest, I thought
it'd all become a pain in the ass.

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:27.640
JULY

00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:24.260
That's what I thought,

00:20:24.510 --> 00:20:28.430
but I thought the embarrassed,
flustered Miyakoshi was entertaining.

00:20:27.770 --> 00:20:32.350
OCTOBER

00:20:28.430 --> 00:20:31.390
And so a change came over
the first "pain in the ass" feeling.

00:20:31.390 --> 00:20:32.350
I don't get it!

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:36.020
Well, even before the incidents,
I thought you were interesting,

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:39.990
so then I had a feeling that
you hadn't really changed since then.

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:43.450
So to be honest,
I can't say that I love you,

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:46.660
but I don't want to let
anyone else have you.

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:51.710
So is that okay? Or no?

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:53.080
It's okay.

00:20:53.710 --> 00:20:56.040
Really? Good.

00:20:56.380 --> 00:20:58.760
- Then we're going out with each other!
- Y-Yeah.

00:20:59.130 --> 00:21:04.720
Being embarrassed about it more than
necessary is creepy, so please don't do that.

00:21:05.010 --> 00:21:06.720
Y-You...

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:10.680
Wh-When a girl kind of likes a guy,
who calls her bashfulness "creepy"?

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:13.440
Is this retribution?

00:21:13.730 --> 00:21:16.730
I'm happy that you're
getting sharper, Miyakoshi.

00:21:18.860 --> 00:21:20.110
All right!

00:21:20.110 --> 00:21:23.070
Various troubles have just fallen away,
so I'm ready to work hard!

00:21:23.070 --> 00:21:25.820
Since I started working here,
I've been through...

00:21:25.820 --> 00:21:27.160
I've been through a lot.

00:21:27.870 --> 00:21:29.700
When I think about it,
I've come a long way.

00:21:29.950 --> 00:21:31.870
You've gone too far!

00:21:32.160 --> 00:21:32.910
I know!

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:37.090
From now on,
my goal is getting back your smile!

00:21:37.710 --> 00:21:41.800
Although saying that, working
a part-time job really isn't that interesting.

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:43.550
Did you just smile?

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:44.510
No.

00:21:45.510 --> 00:21:47.470
But speaking of smiles, Miyakoshi...

00:21:47.720 --> 00:21:50.810
yours has been unnaturally stiff
for the past six months.

00:21:51.390 --> 00:21:52.980
Well, even before that,

00:21:53.310 --> 00:21:55.230
your customer service smile
was always eerie.

00:21:55.230 --> 00:21:56.100
Wha...

00:21:56.100 --> 00:21:58.690
Please work with a natural smile
on your face.

00:21:58.690 --> 00:22:01.480
You're the one person who has
no business saying that to me!

00:23:17.480 --> 00:23:20.110
You don't even have
a customer service smile!

00:23:20.110 --> 00:23:21.190
Yeah, yeah.

00:23:21.610 --> 00:23:23.940
A customer is leaving. If you would...

00:23:26.860 --> 00:23:28.450
Natural, natural...

00:23:29.660 --> 00:23:30.990
Thank you!

00:23:32.740 --> 00:23:35.330
We look forward to your next visit!
